# Passbolt naxsi whitelist - hand-written, NOT a community-maintained
# ruleset (none exists for Passbolt, unlike wordpress_whitelist.rules).
# Scoped narrowly to fix confirmed false positives from real traffic in
# naxsi_error.log; only extend when a new false positive is confirmed
# there, not speculatively.

# Passbolt's API (CakePHP) uses bracket notation for nested/dynamic
# query param names: contain[role], filter[has-users],
# contain[Permission][User], etc. Keys are arbitrary and can't be
# enumerated like WordPress's fixed param names, so each "[" or "]" in
# a param NAME was scoring $XSS 4+4=8 (rules 1310/1311) and blocking
# almost every API call. Whitelisted in the NAME zone only - actual
# submitted values are still fully scanned.
BasicRule wl:1310,1311 "mz:ARGS|NAME";
